.TH WORDCOUNT 1 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int wordCount(FILE *" file ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount()
function reads through the open file stream
.I file
and counts the number of lines, words, and characters it contains,
storing the results in the integers pointed to by
.IR lines ", " words ", and " chars .
This behaves similarly to the standard
.BR wc (1)
utility.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 on failure (for example, if
.I file
is NULL).
